# Sending a file's exact bytes as the body -- a "< path" line (JetBrains
# HTTP Client's own convention) is replaced with that file's raw content
# at send time, byte-for-byte, no pre-request script needed. See
# doc/http-file-format.md's "File uploads" section.
#
# A relative path resolves against the current working directory (same
# rule as everywhere else httpfly reads from disk) -- run this from inside
# doc/examples/, where 8_photo.png sits.
#
# Run `make httpbin-up` first.

###
# @name RawUpload
PUT http://localhost:8080/put HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: image/png

< ./8_photo.png

###
# @name MultipartUpload
# The same "< path" line works inside one part of a multipart body, mixed
# freely with plain text fields (see 5_forms.http for forms without a file).
POST http://localhost:8080/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="avatar"; filename="8_photo.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./8_photo.png
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="username"

alice
--WebAppBoundary--
